From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: pinetab2: more vdd_cpu margin at the low OPPs

The tablet resets - a silent power-on reset - whenever cpufreq steps
vdd_cpu (a TCS4525) while the cores are under heavy NEON load; the same
load survives indefinitely with the frequency pinned, and survives
frequency changes as soon as the OPP table is made voltage-flat. Neither
a settling margin, nor forced PWM mode on the regulator, nor a slower
i2c0 makes a difference, so it is the size of the voltage step that this
board cannot take under load. Lift the low OPPs so no step is larger than
50 mV: 408-816 MHz at 950 mV, 1104 MHz at 1.0 V, 1416 MHz at 1.05 V,
1608 MHz at 1.1 V.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
diff -ruN op_a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi op_b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi	2026-09-19 06:23:36.494639300 +0200
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi	2026-09-19 06:23:36.516164368 +0200
@@ -281,6 +281,28 @@
 	cpu-supply = <&vdd_cpu>;
 };
 
+/* This board cannot take large vdd_cpu steps under load, see the patch. */
+&cpu0_opp_table {
+	opp-408000000 {
+		opp-microvolt = <950000 950000 1150000>;
+	};
+	opp-600000000 {
+		opp-microvolt = <950000 950000 1150000>;
+	};
+	opp-816000000 {
+		opp-microvolt = <950000 950000 1150000>;
+	};
+	opp-1104000000 {
+		opp-microvolt = <1000000 1000000 1150000>;
+	};
+	opp-1416000000 {
+		opp-microvolt = <1050000 1050000 1150000>;
+	};
+	opp-1608000000 {
+		opp-microvolt = <1100000 1100000 1150000>;
+	};
+};
+
 &cru {
 	assigned-clocks = <&pmucru CLK_RTC_32K>, <&cru PLL_GPLL>,
 			  <&pmucru PLL_PPLL>, <&cru PLL_VPLL>;
